WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Hello, I'm Mr. Red.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.880
A horse is a horse, of course, of course, and no one can talk to a horse, of course,

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.520
that is, of course, unless the horse is the famous Mr. Red.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.320
Go right to the source and ask the horse, he'll give you the answer that you endorse.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:31.320
He's always on a steady course, talk to Mr. Red.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.320
Hooray!

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:41.320
Wilbur, here's the...

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:56.320
All right, girls, at the sound of the bell, I want you both to come out fighting.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.320
I'm going to listen to my husband and come as a hunchback of Notre Dame.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.320
Why didn't you tell me you were coming as carmen?

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:07.320
Well, I've been trying to phone you since last night, but your line's been busy.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.320
That's funny.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:15.320
You haven't used the phone.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.320
I thought so.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.320
Wilbur, you left the phone off the hook in the barn again.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.320
Must have been that horse.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.320
I mean, he must have knocked it off accidentally.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.320
I'll go and look.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.320
Excuse me.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.320
Is Wilbur coming to the pageant?

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.320
No.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:31.320
Is Roger?

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.320
No, I'm meeting with a little resistance.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:37.320
As soon as I bring up the subject, he locks himself in the bathroom.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.320
It's no fun without Wilbur.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.320
I wish I could think of some way to convince him to come along.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.320
Well, there is a way, darling.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:45.320
What?

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:50.320
Before I tell you, one of us will have to resign from the Carmen Club.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.320
Well?

00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:08.320
Hey!

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.320
You left the phone off the hook again.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.320
So I made a mistake.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.320
I'm only human.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.320
Why do you keep using that phone?

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.320
I get lonely here all by myself.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.320
Yeah, well, Carol is blaming me, and I'm getting tired of your negligence.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.320
Ed, it is time you and I had a man-to-man talk.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.320
Okay.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:33.320
Take off the apron.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.320
Well, I was just helping Carol with the dishes.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.320
Wilbur!

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.320
Yes, Roger?

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.320
Now, don't let me interrupt your work.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.320
I thought maybe you might like to play golf Saturday.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.320
Not a bad idea.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.320
Now, the girls will be leaving for that parade about 12.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:51.320
We can tell them how beautiful they look, how sorry we are we can't join them,

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.320
and then laugh all the way to the golf course.

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.320
What do you say?

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.320
Great.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.320
See you later.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:05.320
Hey, you know it's impossible to get you on the telephone?

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:11.320
Uh-oh.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:14.320
Ed, if you use that phone once more, I am pulling it out.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.320
You understand?

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.320
Yes, master.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:36.320
You forgot your apron, honey.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.320
Hey, what do you think? Isn't it beautiful?

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:39.320
It's gorgeous.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.320
Oh, darling, you'll make a beautiful lane.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.320
Oh, thanks.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.320
But what good is a lane without Sir Lancelot?

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.320
Here's the book.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.320
Just do what I told you.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.320
Tell him he looks like Sir Lancelot.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.320
But he doesn't.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.320
Wilbur's too smart.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.320
You can't soft-soap him.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.320
It'll work.

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.320
Maybe with your husband, but not with mine.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.320
Oh, for heaven's sake, Carol.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.320
Here he comes now.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:03.320
Oh, good.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.320
Oh, hi, Wilbur.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.320
Hi, honey.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:07.320
Look, look at my new costume.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:16.320
Oh, that's beautiful.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.320
What's the matter?

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:21.320
I'm having quite a resemblance.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.320
What, what, what?

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.320
Here, let me see your profile.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.320
Oh, I wouldn't have believed it.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:26.320
Carol, wait till you see.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:29.320
It is simply the most marvelous thing I've ever seen in all my life.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.320
Let me see the other side.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.320
Just as good from the other side.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:33.320
Oh, it's just marvelous.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:34.320
Oh, here, do you have it?

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:35.320
Goodbye, Kate.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.320
Thank you very much.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:41.320
Yeah.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.320
Same face.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:47.320
It's the same face, but I'll tell you what it is, dear.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:51.320
Oh, for heaven's sake.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.320
What, what, what's the resemblance?

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:54.320
Oh, it's silly.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:57.320
What, what, what, what's silly?

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.320
Kate says you look just like Sir Lancelot.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:15.320
What's so silly about that?

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:17.320
Same face.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:21.320
Well, well, in that light, there is a resemblance.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:31.320
I mean, if I had a spear in my hand, there'd be no doubt about it.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.320
Get up, Merlin.

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:33.320
Here's your spear, honey.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.320
Thank you.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.320
That's no way to hand anybody a spear.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.320
With a spear, the straw goes at that end.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:43.320
Coward!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.320
Oh, that's wonderful, honey.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.320
Now, would you show Harold Jensen how to hold a spear?

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.320
Harold Jensen?

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:53.320
You're going to let Harold Jensen be your knight at the pageant?

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:56.320
Oh, he doesn't look anything like me.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.320
No, he doesn't, dear.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.320
I mean, whoever heard about pot-bellied Sir Lancelot?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.320
Charge!

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.320
Please listen to me.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.320
I've got to find a Don Jose by tomorrow.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.320
Oh, my dear, how about me?

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.320
Oh, you're not listening.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.320
I...

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:16.320
You?

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:17.320
Of course.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.320
I'd make a beautiful toreador.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:20.320
Ah-ha, toro.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.320
Vamos, torito.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.320
Ah-ha, oh, yee.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:26.320
Oh, Addison, I'd have never dreamed of asking you, but you'd be perfect.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.320
Why, naturally.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:32.320
I have the figure, the bearing, the carriage, and look at these legs.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.320
Can you imagine these two beauties in silk stockings?

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.320
Oh, Addison, thank you so much.

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.320
My dear, think nothing of it, because I won't be there.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:44.320
Addison, that was a dirty trick leading me on.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:49.320
My dear, you're going to have to find another Don Jose, because this bullfighter is going to play golf Saturday.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:52.320
Very well.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.320
I won't go to the pageant.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:56.320
Suit yourself, my dear.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:01.320
I'm going to go on the biggest shopping spree you ever saw.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.320
Where do I go for my Don Jose costume?

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.320
Hello, Ed.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.320
Hmm.

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:12.320
What's new?

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.320
Don't know.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:18.320
I missed the morning newscast.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:20.320
I tried to catch up with you, Wilbur.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.320
Hello, Roger.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:23.320
What are you limping for?

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:28.320
Oh, I was practicing putting in my backyard for our game tomorrow, and I twisted my ankle.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:29.320
Oh, that's a shame.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:31.320
I was looking forward to beating you, too.

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:32.320
Sorry, old man.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:33.320
Hello, Roger.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:34.320
Hello, Carol.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.320
Honey, your costume will be ready in about 30 minutes.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:38.320
Oh.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.320
Good.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.320
Costume?

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.320
Didn't he tell you?

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.320
No.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:46.320
He's going to be Sir Lancelot in the pageant.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.320
Him?

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:48.320
Celeste?

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.320
Oh, boy.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.320
What's so funny?

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.320
Kay is waiting for you to try on your costume.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:58.320
His costume?

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.320
Didn't he tell you?

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:00.320
No.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:03.320
Well, he's coming as Don Jose, the bullfighter.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:07.320
Oh.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.320
Oh, I forgot something.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.320
Don Jose, the bullfighter.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:14.320
Hey, that's cute.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:15.320
How did you get roped into this?

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:17.320
Kay hit me in my weak spot, my money belt.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:18.320
How about you?

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.320
Just stupidity.

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:21.320
See you later, Lancelot.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:29.320
Bye, Don Jose.

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.320
Don Jose.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.320
Lancelot.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:35.320
What fools these mortals be.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:39.320
Ed, there are times when a man has to give in to his wife.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:45.320
No wife of mine would make me parade five miles in a hot sun.

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:50.320
Wilbur, here's part of the outfit Miss Ed's going to wear.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:55.320
Oh, so Ed is going to march in the parade, too, huh?

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:00.320
Well, Elaine and Sir Lancelot need a horse, so I figured we might as well use Miss Ed.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:01.320
Good idea.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:08.320
I mean, after all, why should we walk five miles in the hot sun when we can ride on the back of good old Ed?

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:09.320
Look, aren't these pretty?

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.320
Bells and tassels and plumes.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:12.320
Yes.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:17.320
You know, we could tie a great big red bow in his tail.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.320
Harold, I want to talk to you.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:22.320
I tried to get you on the phone, but your line was busy.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.320
Look.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:26.320
Wilbur.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:29.320
That does it.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.320
I warned you.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:32.320
What?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:33.320
I warned you.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.320
I did.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:43.320
I warned her that if I did this once more, I'd take the phone out, and I'm going to.

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.320
Hello, operator.

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:49.320
I would like to have an extension phone removed, please.

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.320
The name is Wilbur Post.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:10:10.320
The address is 17340 Valley Boulevard.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:12.320
Charge!

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.320
Hey!

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.320
What are you doing?

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.320
Sorry, I was practicing with my spear.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.320
That's nice, sonny.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:22.320
Oh, will you tell your mother the telephone man is here to take out the phone?

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:23.320
Hmm?

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:24.320
Hmm?

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:30.320
Look, I'm Mr. Post, the owner.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.320
The phone is in the bar.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.320
Oh, right over there.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.320
Thank you.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.320
Why are we whispering?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.320
I don't want him to know the phone is coming out.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.320
You don't?

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:45.320
Who?

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:48.320
The horse.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:49.320
The horse?

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:52.320
He doesn't want the phone to come out.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:53.320
The horse doesn't?

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:54.320
That's right.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:11:01.320
Look, sonny, will you play with your spear and let me get the phone out?

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:12.320
Leave that phone alone.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:18.320
Hello, stupid.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.320
Who's that?

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.320
Where are you?

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.320
On the roof.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.320
Do you want the phone in or out?

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:26.320
In.

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:31.320
Go home.

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:32.320
What are you doing?

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:33.320
Playing games with me?

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:34.320
Playing games?

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:35.320
Yeah.

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:38.320
First you tell me to leave the phone in, then you tell me to pull it out?

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:39.320
Make up your mind, will you?

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:42.320
Oh, well, I'm sorry. There's been a misunderstanding.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:45.320
You can take the phone out.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:55.320
I must have done something real bad when I was a kid.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:59.320
Ed, that phone is going out.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:03.320
If it does, I don't walk in the parade.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.320
Is that supposed to be a threat?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:10.320
You can ride on a big dog for all I care.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:13.320
You are going to be in that parade.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:20.320
You'll have to carry me.

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:22.320
Oh, Carol, you look lovely.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:23.320
Oh, thank you.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.320
So do you.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:25.320
Thank you.

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.320
Where's Roger?

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:30.320
Oh, he's right...

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:38.320
Oh, Addison, come on in.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:44.320
Kate, if I didn't go, how much shopping would you do?

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:49.320
Six hours and four credit cards.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:57.320
Olé.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:00.320
This is the last time I buy a suit off the rack.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:12.320
At last, they're putting men up in cans.

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:15.320
Wilbur, all we can do is pray for rain.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:20.320
Please. This suit is not guaranteed against rust.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:30.320
When I'm ready, you better get Mr. Ed dressed.

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.320
My lance locked.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:35.320
Uh-oh, here he comes.

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:53.320
I'm going to teach that phone puller a lesson.

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:58.320
Come on, Ed, it's time for the parade.

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:00.320
It's growing dark.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.320
Where is everybody?

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.320
Ed, they're waiting. I've got to get you dressed.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:10.320
Is that you, Mother?

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.320
Get up and stop horsing around.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:16.320
I hear voices, but not on the phone.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.320
Ed, for the last time...

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:23.320
Please, you're yelling at a sick horse.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.320
I brought some extra milk.

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:26.320
What's wrong with Mr. Ed?

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:31.320
He is perfectly all right.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:34.320
Wilbur, he's coughing. Maybe I better call a vet.

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:38.320
There is nothing wrong with him.

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:40.320
Then why is he coughing?

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.320
He's faking, Carol. Believe me.

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.320
Oh, honey, I know you're thinking of me,

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.320
but we can't go off and leave Mr. Ed when he's sick like that.

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.320
There'll be other pageants. Let's forget about it.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:51.320
I'll go call a vet.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:55.320
No, Carol, please.

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:58.320
Oh, that was a dirty trick.

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:01.320
Are you going to let her miss that parade?

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:03.320
Is that you, Mother?

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:05.320
Mother?

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:08.320
Oh, brother.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:12.320
I absolutely refuse to wear this ridiculous ponytail.

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.320
But darling, all bullfighters wear that funny little hairpiece.

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:17.320
Some of them also get gored, but we've got to stop some place.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.320
Okay.

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:21.320
I have bad news. Mr. Ed is sick.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:23.320
Oh, the poor thing.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:26.320
We can't leave him alone, so you two better go on without us.

00:15:26.320 --> 00:15:29.320
He's not missing the pageant.

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.320
I'm afraid so.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:35.320
Well, well, how do you feel today, old fella?

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:37.320
Oh!

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:42.320
Oh!

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:45.320
Hmm? Doesn't look bad at all.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:49.320
Nice color.

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:52.320
Huh? Lymph nodes feel all right.

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:55.320
I still say he's faking.

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:57.320
You better not be too sure of that, Mr. Post.

00:15:57.320 --> 00:16:00.320
After all, the poor thing can't talk, you know.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:06.320
But...

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:08.320
Is he all right, Doctor?

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.320
Heart feels fine.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.320
Sounds very good.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:19.320
I think all this fellow needs is a good shot of vitamins.

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:23.320
Now, be afraid, old fellow.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.320
Dr. Connors isn't going to hurt you.

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:31.320
This won't hurt one bit, though.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:33.320
I told you he was all right.

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.320
Come on, honey, you better tell the Addison's.

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:37.320
Doctor, do you think he's all right to leave for a few hours?

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:39.320
Oh, he seems fine.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:40.320
Well, if you're sure...

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.320
Come on, honey.

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:46.320
PHONE RINGS

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:48.320
Hello?

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:52.320
Oh, hi, Wilbur.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.320
Really?

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:57.320
Wonderful.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:02.320
Oh, Addison, the horse is all right, and we're going to the pageant.

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:04.320
Lee?

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:05.320
Mr. Ed.

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:07.320
Oh, come on. Don't worry.

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:09.320
Dr. Connors knows what he's doing.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.320
Mr. Post! Mr. Post!

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.320
Mr. Post!

00:17:13.320 --> 00:17:15.320
What happened?

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.320
Your horse pushed me down.

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:20.320
I think he wanted to sit on me.

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:23.320
Wilbur, I just knew there was something wrong with Mr. Ed.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.320
But he showed no symptoms at all.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:29.320
He must be psychologically disturbed.

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.320
Doctor, do you know of any horse-sitting service?

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.320
Honey, that's a wonderful idea.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:37.320
Doctor, would you mind staying with Mr. Ed till we get back?

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:40.320
Well, I could be back, but it would cost you so much.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:42.320
It'll be worth it.

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:44.320
Honey, I know how much this pageant means to you.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:46.320
Yes, but we still need a horse.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:48.320
I'll rent one from the Brunswick Stables.

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:51.320
They're right down the road. You call the Addisons. I'll be right back.

00:17:51.320 --> 00:17:53.320
Come on, Doctor.

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:58.320
So they got someone else.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:01.320
Well, I'll fix him.

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.320
Oh, Carol, hold still, will you? You're rigging like a fish.

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:05.320
Would you please get that?

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:08.320
I can't get the pin in. Wait a minute, will you?

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:10.320
Let me know if I hit your brain.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:11.320
Did I?

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:12.320
I'm Dr. Connors.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.320
How do you do, Doctor? Come in.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:15.320
Hello, Doctor.

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.320
Sorry I couldn't get here any sooner.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.320
Oh, we really appreciate you coming back.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:19.320
That's perfectly all right.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:21.320
Excuse me. I'll call my husband.

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:26.320
Wilbur! Dr. Connors is here.

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:28.320
Coming, honey.

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:43.320
Giddyap, Josephine.

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:45.320
Honey, look!

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:51.320
Now we can't go.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:54.320
What's the use? I better tell the Addisons.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.320
Don't call us. We'll call you.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.320
Come, Carmen.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:09.320
Well, I'll tell Dr. Connors we don't need him anymore.

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:15.320
Hello, Miss Dad.

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.320
How do you feel, huh?

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:21.320
Oh, you've had a rough day, haven't you?

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.320
I know what was the matter with you.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:26.320
You were lonesome, weren't you?

00:19:26.320 --> 00:19:29.320
Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:33.320
Oh, you're a good horse.

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.320
Honey.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.320
I didn't know you liked Ed that much.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:42.320
Well, I feel sorry for him.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:46.320
I'll bet if he knew how happy it would make you,

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:48.320
he'd want to go to the pageant.

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:53.320
Well, I just wonder if he's well enough.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.320
Look!

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.320
He's his old self again.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.320
He is.

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.320
Tell the Addisons.

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:02.320
All right.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:03.320
You tell them.

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.320
Okay.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:09.320
Let's tell them together.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:17.320
Good morning, Ed.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:19.320
Good morning.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:20.320
I've been thinking, Ed.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:23.320
That was a real nice gesture going to the pageant yesterday.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.320
It sure was.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.320
You know, if you promise to behave,

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:29.320
I'll put the phone back in the barn, okay?

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:31.320
You've got my word.

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:33.320
Okay, I'll go in the house and call the company.

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:37.320
Wilbur, use the phone in the office.

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:39.320
Okay.

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:52.320
Hey.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:55.320
Who phoned the company to put this back?

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.320
Ed?

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.320
It's growing dark.

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:03.320
Where is everybody?

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:06.320
Is that you, Mother?

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.320
Hmm?

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:12.320
JAPOAN

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:42.120
Booyakity yak a streak and waste your time a day

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:46.620
But Mr. Ed will never speak unless he has something to say

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:48.920
A horse is a horse, of course, of course

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:51.120
And this one will talk till his voice is hoarse

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.620
You never heard of a talking horse?

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:57.120
Well, listen to this!

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:01.620
I am Mr. Ed

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:04.620
The End

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:07.620
This has been a Filmways television presentation.
